{"name":"Regalia","hex":"#522d80","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"regalia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Royal rights, prerogatives and privileges actually enjoyed by any sovereign, regardless of his title (emperor, grand duke etc.).","The emblems, symbols, or paraphernalia indicative of royalty or any other sovereign status; such as a crown, orb, sceptre or sword."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of large cigar of superior quality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regalia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Regalia","blocks":[{"text":"Regalia is the set of emblems, symbols, or paraphernalia indicative of royal status, as well as rights, prerogatives and privileges enjoyed by a sovereign, regardless of title. The word originally referred to the elaborate formal dress and accessories of a sovereign, but now it also refers to any type of elaborate formal dress. The word stems from the Latin substantivation of the adjective regalis, \"regal\", itself from rex, \"king\". It is sometimes used in the singular, regale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Aachen_city_hall_Imperial_Regalia_replicas.jpg/330px-Aachen_city_hall_Imperial_Regalia_replicas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regalia"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Bav_Regaliaaa.jpg/500px-Bav_Regaliaaa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Bav_Regaliaaa.jpg/500px-Bav_Regaliaaa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Regalia of the past kings of Bavaria, Residenz Palace treasury, Munich","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABav_Regaliaaa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Crown%2C_Sword_and_Globus_Cruciger_of_Hungary2.jp